[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Divide and Conquer with Binary Search Variants"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Binary search is one of the most fundamental algorithms in computer science. While standard binary search looks for an exact match in a sorted array, understanding its variants allows developers to solve complex optimization and search space problems efficiently."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Core Concepts of Binary Search Variants"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"The divide and conquer paradigm underpins binary search. By repeatedly dividing the search space in half, we reduce the time complexity from O(N) to O(log N). Variants generally fall into three categories: finding the lower bound, finding the upper bound, and searching in rotated or monotonic predicate spaces."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Lower Bound: Finds the first element that is greater than or equal to a target value."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Upper Bound: Finds the first element that is strictly greater than a target value."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Predicate Search: Optimizes parameters over a monotonic boolean function."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Implementing the Lower Bound Variant"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Below is a Python implementation of the lower bound variant. Notice how the pointers adjust based on the condition rather than an exact equality check."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"def lower_bound(arr, target):
    left, right = 0, len(arr)
    while left < right:
        mid = left + (right - left) // 2
        if arr[mid] >= target:
            right = mid
        else:
            left = mid + 1
    return left"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices and Common Pitfalls"},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Integer Overflow: Always compute mid as left + (right - left) // 2 instead of (left + right) // 2 in languages with fixed-size integers."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Infinite Loops: Ensure that the search space strictly decreases in every iteration by adjusting pointers with +1 or -1 when appropriate."},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"Mastering these binary search variants enables you to tackle difficult algorithmic challenges, particularly those disguised as minimization or maximization problems."}]
